WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:09.000
Wie sprichst du mit der jüngeren Generationen im Kibbutz über das, was passiert ist?

00:14.933 --> 00:15.666
Firstly,

00:15.666 --> 00:19.366
as the person that was head of education at the kibbutz,

00:19.366 --> 00:21.200
this was what I was doing

00:22.133 --> 00:27.600
throughout the year-and-a-half after October 7,

00:27.766 --> 00:29.000
it was,

00:29.733 --> 00:30.733
firstly...

00:30.733 --> 00:31.933
If you speak about the kibbutz,

00:31.933 --> 00:33.800
kibbutz is like a community,

00:33.800 --> 00:37.533
so the first thing we wanted to do is to make them feel,

00:37.533 --> 00:40.166
like get them back on their feet after October 7th,

00:40.166 --> 00:42.133
because they were in a very,

00:42.133 --> 00:43.700
very bad situation...

00:43.933 --> 00:46.033
We’re talking about children and teenagers,

00:46.600 --> 00:48.000
and you have to understand,

00:48.333 --> 00:50.300
that children and teenagers here,

00:50.800 --> 00:52.166
some of them...

00:52.833 --> 00:55.766
saw their parents or siblings

00:56.400 --> 01:00.300
get shot and die in front of their eyes.

01:00.666 --> 01:02.466
some of them...

01:02.466 --> 01:05.466
there were four teenagers that were murdered

01:05.466 --> 01:06.433
in the kibbutz.

01:06.733 --> 01:09.100
There was one teenager that was kidnapped,

01:09.500 --> 01:11.466
there was a child that was kidnapped,

01:12.600 --> 01:16.666
there were families that were completely broken.

01:18.066 --> 01:21.400
I can tell you about one teenager,

01:22.000 --> 01:22.900
that...

01:23.300 --> 01:25.233
when the head of security

01:25.966 --> 01:28.933
came to his house in the morning...

01:28.933 --> 01:31.966
he found there was a kid that was jogging.

01:32.400 --> 01:33.566
October 7...

01:33.566 --> 01:35.300
6:30 in the morning,

01:35.300 --> 01:37.333
there was a kid that went jogging.

01:37.333 --> 01:39.200
A twelve-and-a-half-year-old,

01:39.700 --> 01:42.900
and the head of security went to find him,

01:43.166 --> 01:45.933
and he didn’t have time to get him back to his house,

01:45.933 --> 01:47.866
so he put him in his own house.

01:48.333 --> 01:50.900
When he turned to get back to the battle,

01:51.100 --> 01:52.400
he was

01:52.400 --> 01:55.700
immediately murdered, it was a very brutal murder.

01:56.333 --> 01:59.666
we know because it took us days to identify the body.

02:00.400 --> 02:01.500
And...

02:01.666 --> 02:05.400
apparently there was a teenager that...

02:05.600 --> 02:07.200
saw the entire thing.

02:07.200 --> 02:11.566
The entire murder through the shutters of her house,

02:11.966 --> 02:14.500
it took us five months to understand

02:14.500 --> 02:16.400
why she doesn’t leave the house

02:16.400 --> 02:19.066
where she was evacuated to.

02:20.166 --> 02:20.933
So the...

02:20.933 --> 02:25.066
the stories of the teenagers, they were in shock,

02:25.066 --> 02:26.633
they were in complete shock.

02:27.066 --> 02:30.966
And what did we do in order to give them the...

02:31.066 --> 02:32.333
When you speak about the kibbutz,

02:32.333 --> 02:33.833
you speak about the community,

02:34.200 --> 02:36.200
when you are a part of a group,

02:36.200 --> 02:38.666
when you have a sense of belonging to a group,

02:38.733 --> 02:41.266
this is a very

02:42.800 --> 02:46.700
essential element for your

02:47.733 --> 02:50.066
recovery from the trauma.

02:50.533 --> 02:53.433
A strong group gives you strong resilience.

02:54.900 --> 02:56.933
So, we really started

02:56.933 --> 03:01.033
on creating that community within them.

03:01.100 --> 03:02.366
we made,

03:02.666 --> 03:04.766
the kibbutz that we were evacuated to,

03:04.766 --> 03:07.633
Mishmar HaEmek, gave us.

03:07.900 --> 03:11.600
the facilities we needed and we just...

03:11.600 --> 03:15.666
they gave us this empty

03:15.900 --> 03:20.200
bomb shelter which looked horrible at the beginning,

03:20.266 --> 03:21.933
but many people came to help,

03:21.933 --> 03:25.266
the people of Mishmar HaEmek are amazing people really.

03:27.133 --> 03:28.733
Many people from there,

03:28.733 --> 03:31.300
and from the surrounding areas came to help,

03:31.300 --> 03:32.800
and we painted and

03:33.533 --> 03:36.466
we made a little nice

03:36.466 --> 03:38.766
warm club for them.

03:38.766 --> 03:41.300
The best we could under the circumstances.

03:45.400 --> 03:48.366
It was unbelievable to see.

03:48.700 --> 03:55.366
As time went by it became their little sanctuary,

03:55.533 --> 03:57.566
they used to come back from school,

03:58.066 --> 03:58.800
Go,

03:58.800 --> 04:02.800
because each family got a small room,

04:03.466 --> 04:06.066
imagine me with my husband,

04:06.066 --> 04:10.300
with my two children with my two dogs in a...

04:10.400 --> 04:14.200
maybe 5 by 5...

04:16.200 --> 04:17.733
unit.

04:18.133 --> 04:20.300
5 meters,

04:20.300 --> 04:21.666
really small.

04:23.800 --> 04:26.700
And teenagers need their privacy,

04:27.366 --> 04:32.433
so they couldn’t find their...

04:35.933 --> 04:38.433
They couldn’t find the place where they could feel,

04:39.300 --> 04:41.800
the quiet they need as teenagers,

04:42.400 --> 04:43.800
and it was unbelievable to see

04:43.800 --> 04:45.700
they used to come back from school,

04:46.200 --> 04:50.700
grab a blanket and go to the club and they would

04:50.700 --> 04:52.866
fall asleep on the sofas,

04:53.533 --> 04:55.100
with other friends...

04:55.100 --> 04:55.966
And they would

04:55.966 --> 04:57.666
Take a nap or...

04:57.733 --> 05:00.566
come and play a nice game with somebody,

05:00.566 --> 05:03.866
and this was theirs and they used to stay there until

05:03.866 --> 05:06.466
every night until 11...

05:06.566 --> 05:11.300
Or 12, even midnight. We wouldn’t allow it,

05:11.300 --> 05:12.866
but since it was a bomb shelter,

05:12.866 --> 05:14.133
we couldn’t lock it,

05:14.133 --> 05:18.133
so they were waiting for us to go to bed,

05:18.133 --> 05:20.466
and they were going in...

05:20.800 --> 05:26.966
sneaking back into the shelter. It was so important to them.

05:27.100 --> 05:30.666
Being together...

05:31.400 --> 05:33.266
Being with one another,

05:33.766 --> 05:37.466
and that was something that we worked very hard on.

05:38.366 --> 05:41.133
There were plenty of teenagers that at first

05:41.133 --> 05:42.700
didn’t come,

05:42.700 --> 05:45.600
didn’t even show up to the activities,

05:45.600 --> 05:50.700
or the gatherings, so what we did, I instructed ...

05:52.133 --> 05:53.466
the guides...

05:53.466 --> 05:56.100
the youth guides that were with them.

05:56.733 --> 06:00.233
I told them, "every different club",

06:02.166 --> 06:03.966
"you take all the children,"

06:03.966 --> 06:07.366
"the list, and you divide it between ... "

06:07.666 --> 06:09.066
"Between the staff."

06:09.533 --> 06:14.666
We brought huge staff to work with them and...

06:14.666 --> 06:17.600
let's say that we had a twenty-something teenagers,

06:17.966 --> 06:21.466
we brought four staff members,

06:21.933 --> 06:25.033
and I divided the children between the staff members,

06:25.266 --> 06:26.133
and I told them,

06:26.133 --> 06:32.466
this is what you do, "you call every child every day",

06:32.533 --> 06:35.166
"you’re not going to speak with them for half an hour",

06:35.166 --> 06:38.066
"you’re going to say three sentences",

06:38.533 --> 06:41.333
"we are at the club, we’re doing this and this today",

06:41.333 --> 06:42.800
"we would be happy to see you."

06:42.800 --> 06:45.766
That's it...

06:45.766 --> 06:48.066
That's it, that's it. Every day.

06:49.366 --> 06:54.600
And by december, it took time...

06:54.600 --> 06:55.533
they were

06:55.533 --> 06:57.533
coming and sniffing around

06:57.533 --> 06:59.066
to see if it fits them or not,

06:59.066 --> 07:02.100
by december we reached,

07:02.100 --> 07:09.566
about 97% of attendance in the in the club,

07:09.566 --> 07:13.700
but it was very hard work by the by the staff and...

07:13.700 --> 07:17.666
another thing that I told them was,

07:17.666 --> 07:20.700
"If you didn’t see a child for like the last month",

07:20.866 --> 07:25.466
"and suddenly he appears, he must have a good experience",

07:25.900 --> 07:28.300
so they were all on it,

07:28.300 --> 07:31.166
they knew each one had the number,

07:31.500 --> 07:34.700
the list of children, that they needed to focus on...

07:34.700 --> 07:36.800
to make sure that they're not going,

07:37.200 --> 07:39.266
to get lost somewhere,

07:39.266 --> 07:41.400
because we did have many of them that broke down

07:41.500 --> 07:44.500
so we were really monitoring.

07:44.566 --> 07:47.700
We had this chart with monitoring

07:48.100 --> 07:51.166
the children if you saw something

07:51.766 --> 07:55.266
that needs to have a special attention,

07:55.933 --> 07:57.866
and it was very important,

07:57.866 --> 08:01.933
because we did have many of them that broke down

08:02.733 --> 08:05.200
throughout the year.

08:06.166 --> 08:09.300
And every person deals with trauma differently,

08:09.300 --> 08:12.566
so I went way beyond your question,

08:14.366 --> 08:16.933
This is something that is very important for me to say,

08:16.933 --> 08:19.566
because I think that we found out

08:19.566 --> 08:22.900
ways to deal with trauma that

08:23.133 --> 08:27.400
In a situation that the world doesn’t really know,

08:27.400 --> 08:30.000
there were very few researches

08:30.000 --> 08:34.300
about this particular situation so...
